msgstr "Bonjour,"

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"I'm %(primary_contact)s, the technical point of contact for the "
"%(product_name)s platform, and I just created a new account for you. To get "
"started, sign in with the button below. Your username is this email address."
msgstr ""
"Je suis %(primary_contact)s, le contact technique de la plateforme "
"%(product_name)s, et je viens de vous créer un compte. Pour commencer, "
"connectez-vous avec le bouton ci-dessous. Votre nom d'utilisateur est cette "
"adresse e-mail."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid "You should receive your password in a separate text-only email."
msgstr ""
"Vous devriez recevoir votre mot de passe dans un autre e-mail, en texte brut."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"You can use the 'Forgot Password' link on the sign-in page to change your "
"password at any time."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez utiliser le lien « Mot de passe oublié ? » de la page de "
"connexion pour changer votre mot de passe à tout moment."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"If you have any questions, email me at <a href=\"mailto:%(support_email)s\" "
"style=\"font-weight:600\">%(support_email)s</a>."
msgstr ""
"Pour toute question, écrivez-moi à <a href=\"mailto:%(support_email)s\" "
"style=\"font-weight:600\">%(support_email)s</a>."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid "What's included:"
msgstr "Ce qui est inclus :"

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>An account on %(product_name)s <a href=\"%(login_url)s\" "
"target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">platform</a></strong> for the duration of "
"this course. Every prompt is a real, billable request to an LLM provider, so "
"please experiment freely, but don't run automated load against it."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Un compte sur la <a href=\"%(login_url)s\" target=\"_blank\" "
"rel=\"noopener\">plateforme</a> %(product_name)s</strong> pendant toute la "
"durée de ce cours. Chaque prompt est une vraie requête, facturée, à un "
"fournisseur de LLM : expérimentez librement, mais ne lui envoyez pas de "
"charge automatisée."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong>Your own AI resources.</strong> You can create, change and delete "
"your own LLMClients, plugins, connections and secrets, and you are "
"encouraged to experiment with them while you are attending this course."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Vos propres ressources d'IA.</strong> Vous pouvez créer, modifier et "
"supprimer vos propres LLMClients, plugins, connexions et secrets, et nous "
"vous encourageons à les expérimenter pendant ce cours."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong>Thousands of LLMs from nine providers:</strong> Anthropic, Cohere, "
"Fireworks AI, Google AI (Gemini), Hugging Face, Meta AI (Llama), Mistral, "
"OpenAI and Together AI, all through a single interface, so that you can "
"compare models hands-on."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Des milliers de LLM de neuf fournisseurs :</strong> Anthropic, "
"Cohere, Fireworks AI, Google AI (Gemini), Hugging Face, Meta AI (Llama), "
"Mistral, OpenAI et Together AI, tous accessibles par une interface unique, "
"pour comparer les modèles en pratique."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong><a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/en/latest/smarter-resources/"
"smarter-llmtool.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Plugins</a> for "
"LLM tool calling</strong> that connect an LLM to SQL databases, remote REST "
"APIs, web search, image search, Agent Skills and static data. Your data "
"stays where it is: the LLM only sees the query results and responses that it "
"asks for. <a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/en/latest/smarter-framework/"
"smarter-extensions.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Extensions</a>, "
"which the platform administrator installs, add tools written in Python."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Des <a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/en/latest/smarter-resources/"
"smarter-llmtool.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">plugins</a> pour "
"l'appel d'outils des LLM</strong>, qui connectent un LLM à des bases de "
"données SQL, des API REST distantes, la recherche web, la recherche "
"d'images, des Agent Skills et des données statiques. Vos données restent où "
"elles sont : le LLM ne voit que les résultats de requêtes et les réponses "
"qu'il demande. Les <a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/en/latest/smarter-"
"framework/smarter-extensions.html\" rel=\"noopener\" "
"target=\"_blank\">extensions</a>, que l'administrateur de la plateforme "
"installe, ajoutent des outils écrits en Python."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>A no-code approach to authoring AI resources.</strong> Every "
"resource in %(product_name)s is a short <a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/en/"
"latest/smarter-framework/smarter-manifests.html\" rel=\"noopener\" "
"target=\"_blank\">YAML manifest</a>, so you can build and manage a working "
"AI application without writing code."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Une approche sans code pour créer des ressources d'IA.</strong> "
"Chaque ressource de %(product_name)s est un court <a href=\"https://"
"docs.smarter.sh/en/latest/smarter-framework/smarter-manifests.html\" "
"rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">manifeste YAML</a> : vous pouvez donc "
"créer et gérer une application d'IA fonctionnelle sans écrire de code."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong>A web Prompt Engineering Workbench</strong> for designing, testing "
"and debugging the prompts of your AI applications interactively."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Un Prompt Engineering Workbench web</strong> pour concevoir, tester "
"et déboguer de façon interactive les prompts de vos applications d'IA."

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid "Open Source, Built for Production"
msgstr "Open source, conçu pour la production"

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>%(product_name)s is more than a teaching tool.</strong> It is free, "
"open source software, licensed under the GNU AGPL v3, and it was built to "
"run in production: on Kubernetes, with cost accounting, secrets management "
"and per-account access control. Running at scale, security and cost "
"management may be out of scope for this course, but you will face them once "
"you complete it, and the source code and documentation are there for you to "
"explore, during the course and after."
msgstr ""
"<strong>%(product_name)s est bien plus qu'un outil pédagogique.</strong> "
"C'est un logiciel libre et open source, sous licence GNU AGPL v3, conçu pour "
"fonctionner en production : sur Kubernetes, avec la comptabilité des coûts, "
"la gestion des secrets et le contrôle d'accès par compte. Le passage à "
"l'échelle, la sécurité et la gestion des coûts dépassent peut-être le cadre "
